# What builds, tools and maintainers leave in the tree. Editor and OS files belong in your own
# core.excludesFile; their sections here are a safety net.

# Rust and Cargo
# Cargo.lock stays tracked (the binaries build with --locked), and so does proptest-regressions/
# (proptest asks for it to be committed). /target has no trailing slash on purpose: a
# directory-only pattern misses a target that is a symlink to another disk.
/target
/fuzz/target
/fuzz/artifacts
**/*.rs.bk

# MSVC debug symbols, rustc crash dumps, cargo-mutants output
*.pdb
rustc-ice-*.txt
**/mutants.out*/

# Release archives (.github/workflows/release.yml packs into dist/)
/dist/

# Insta snapshots waiting for review; accepted *.snap files are tracked
*.snap.new
*.pending-snap

# cargo-fuzz: new inputs stay in corpus-new/ until they join the tracked fuzz/corpus/
/fuzz/corpus-new/
/fuzz/coverage/

# Coverage and profiling output (criterion and nextest write under target/)
*.profraw
*.profdata
lcov.info
tarpaulin-report.*
flamegraph*.svg
perf.data
perf.data.old

# Secrets and local environment (wrangler reads .dev.vars and .env)
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.dev.vars*
!.dev.vars.example

# Private keys and certificates; public keys stay trackable
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
!*.pub

# Logs, temporary and backup files
*.log
*.tmp
*.swp
*.swo
*~
*.orig
*.rej

# Editors and IDEs: per-user settings carry absolute paths
.idea/
.vscode/
.vs/
.zed/

# Operating systems
.DS_Store
._*
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini

# Python and Node tooling (scripts/)
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
node_modules/

# Cloudflare Pages deploys (npx wrangler pages deploy site)
.wrangler/

# task worktrees (controller-managed)
.worktrees/
